{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/imr4g3","slideIndex":2,"text":"Source: SYSTEM_DIAGRAM.md and the current backend pipeline. YOLO segmentation proposes Aadhaar document boundaries; OpenCV proposes geometric quadrilaterals and helps rectify perspective. PaddleOCR supplies text and word-level coordinates, while the separate YOLO number detector supplies an additional number-region proposal. The verification stage checks the twelve-digit shape, the first-digit rule, Verhoeff checksum and Aadhaar-specific context. The checksum alone does not prove identity. The app masks digits 1–8, runs OCR on the masked result, and returns a flattened PDF only when the audit passes; uncertain inputs fail closed."}
