{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/lrjr3c","slideIndex":3,"text":"Exact checkpoint sizes come from backend/models and CTO_APPLICATION_GUIDE.md. The base files are the official Ultralytics YOLO26 nano segmentation and detection weights. Ultralytics model.train() fine-tuned the task-specific weights and heads. The document model used 20 epochs, 384 px, batch 8, freezing the first five layers. The final number model continued from the earlier custom number checkpoint for 15 more epochs at 512 px and batch 4 with all layers trainable. Per task, the generated set had 180 train, 36 validation and 36 test images; no real Aadhaar records were used. The .pt extension marks a PyTorch checkpoint, not pytest. The reported disk size covers only the checkpoint files, not PyTorch, PaddleOCR and other runtime components. Check Ultralytics commercial licensing before external deployment. Official documentation: https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolo26 ; https://docs.ultralytics.com/tasks/segment ; https://docs.ultralytics.com/tasks/detect ."}
